Upgrade procedure for wireguard-tools

Source: https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-tools/ (tag vVERSION, e.g.
v1.0.20260223).  Tarballs are also available from
https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-tools/snapshot/wireguard-tools-VERSION.tar.xz
but a snapshot omits files marked export-ignore, so prefer a git checkout.
The release tags are signed by Jason A. Donenfeld
(AB99 42E6 D4A4 CFC3 4126  20A7 49FC 7012 A5DE 03AE); verify with
"git tag -v vVERSION".

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Clone the repository and export the tag:
     git --work-tree=/tmp/wg-export checkout vVERSION -- .
2. Use the vendor-update skill (branch vendor/wireguard-tools, prefix
   contrib/wireguard-tools).
3. The vendor branch holds the contents of upstream's src/ directory at its
   top level, pruned of everything listed in .gitignore (the same layout
   FreeBSD uses): Makefile, completion/, fuzz/, ipc-uapi-windows.h,
   ipc-windows.h, netlink.h, uapi/, wg-quick/, wincompat/, ipc-linux.h,
   ipc-openbsd.h, man/wg-quick.8 and systemd/.  Keep the .gitignore
   file itself.  Stage with "git add -A -f".
4. git subtree merge -P contrib/wireguard-tools <vendor-branch>
5. Build glue lives in usr.bin/wg (identical to FreeBSD's).  Check it
   against FreeBSD's usr.bin/wg for new source files or flags.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  None.  1.0.20260223 is carried unmodified.

  FreeBSD carries one patch, e95cf8b04b47 "wg: ipc: add allowed-ip flags
  support for FreeBSD" (ipc-freebsd.h, in the allowed-ips loop of
  kernel_set_device: replace the "TODO: implement me" -EOPNOTSUPP block
  with nvlist_add_number(nvl_aips[j], "flags", aip->flags)).  It is NOT
  applied here because sys/dev/wg in this tree does not implement the
  per-allowed-ip "flags" nvlist key (WGALLOWEDIP_REMOVE_ME).  Applying it
  would make "wg set ... allowed-ips -ip" silently add the address instead
  of removing it.  Apply it when sys/dev/wg gains that support (FreeBSD
  commits 684dd4e8c008 and related).

Notes:
  - ipc.c selects ipc-freebsd.h with defined(__FreeBSD__); our compilers
    define both __FreeBSD__ and __MidnightBSD__, so no change is needed.
  - ipc-freebsd.h includes <dev/wg/if_wg.h> from the system headers.
